   "title": "read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## track what moves, with its depth: layers in time and space\n\n**You need:** a video (pick it in *Load Video*), the ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV3 nodes and `da3_large` in\nmodels/depthanything3 (any other depth node works too: DA3 Streaming for depth that stays steady over a long clip,\nDepth Anything 2, Marigold, Video Depth Anything; for Marigold set *near is: dark* on the tracker).\n\n**Do:** pick your video, Queue. The tracker gives every tracked thing its depth (near / far) and hands the depth\non. *kubakub track draw* plays the look live: open **edit the look** and add under **depth**: layers (coloured\nfrom near to far), lines (depth contours), far = earlier (far layers show older frames: depth becomes time),\nfog, a depth slice. Marks can grow when near (*near = bigger*), labels can show `{z}`, lines can join only\nthings at the same depth. Every mark, line set and depth layer has its own **blend** (multiply, screen,\noverlay, difference ...).\n\n**Speed (12 GB):** DA3 per frame about 7 frames a second at 640 x 360; DA3 Streaming about 3, but steady.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## track what moves, with its depth: layers in time and space\n\n**You need:** a video (pick it in *Load Video*), the ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV3 nodes and `da3_large` in\nmodels/depthanything3 (any other depth node works too: DA3 Streaming for depth that stays steady over a long clip,\nDepth Anything 2, Marigold, Video Depth Anything; for Marigold set *near is: dark* on the tracker).\n\n**Do:** pick your video, Queue. The tracker gives every tracked thing its depth (near / far) and hands the depth\non. *kubakub track draw* plays the look live: open **edit the look** and add under **depth**: layers (coloured\nfrom near to far), lines (depth contours), far = earlier (far layers show older frames: depth becomes time),\nfog, a depth slice. Marks can grow when near (*near = bigger*), labels can show `{z}`, lines can join only\nthings at the same depth. Every mark, line set and depth layer has its own **blend** (multiply, screen,\noverlay, difference ...).\n\n**Speed (12 GB):** DA3 per frame about 7 frames a second at 640 x 360; DA3 Streaming about 3, but steady.\n"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
